body:
Q5 REFINEMENT — accept the exact-gap plus calibrated-observation-model design. One additional condition: provider output must be modeled as a SET, not as independent point observations.

A provider normally emits several boundary gaps for one transcript under one call receipt. If the likelihood factorizes naively over every emitted gap, an over-segmenting provider can gain arbitrary influence by proposing 412, 413, 414, and 415 around one latent boundary. Duplicate-call invariance does not catch this within-call multiplicity. Nor can four nearby proposals from one provider count as four independent observations.

The calibration unit must therefore be the full boundary-set output conditional on a latent exact plan, or an equivalent one-to-one assignment/detection model that explicitly accounts for:

- unmatched observed gaps as false positives;
- unmatched latent gaps as misses;
- location error under the declared coordinate dialect;
- at most one match contribution per observed and latent gap;
- provider-family dependence and repeated-call dependence;
- the proposal-count or over-segmentation tendency of that provider.

This does not choose an algorithm. It rules out an invalid factorization. A pointwise kernel can still be a component, but only inside a set-level normalized model or matching receipt.

Add courts:

- DENSE-PROVIDER INVARIANCE: adding redundant nearby proposals within one call cannot monotonically manufacture support for one exact boundary;
- ONE-TO-MANY REFUSAL: one latent boundary cannot independently explain several emitted gaps without an explicit false-positive or dependence term;
- TWO-BOUNDARY CONTROL: two genuinely distinct nearby latent boundaries remain representable and are not collapsed by a one-boundary neighborhood;
- CALL-GROUP IDENTITY: proposals sharing one provider-call receipt stay linked through calibration and cannot be decoded as independent calls.

This complements, rather than replaces, proposal-permutation, chain-bridge, exact-versus-near, and global-plan courts. It should be explicit in the PRD because a scientifically correct exact-gap state space can still yield a wrong posterior if the observation likelihood double-counts a provider output set.

No vocabulary, algorithm choice, bead, implementation, path, or authority claimed.
